Z||000003||Wolfhound||05-18-2001||04:04 PM||||Bruce, I just when out and looked at an old column. It appears that the tube is telescopic but the steering shaft doesn't appear to be. let me check closer and I'll get back shortly. I,ll go bang around on it a bit, its a throw away column.<BR>Coy<P>OK, It is. <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/column.JPG"> <BR>Note in the photo the the tube is telescopic and can move about 5 inches before the lower attachment points hit the larger tube. The shaft is solid from the steering wheel and is fitted with a matching tube. a probe in the tube portion measures about 8 inches.<BR> Is this a kit application? Spyder maybe. <p>[This message has been edited by Wolfhound (edited 05-18-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||bcwawright||05-18-2001||08:52 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Wolfhound:<BR><B>Bruce, I just when out and looked at an old column. It appears that the tube is telescopic but the steering shaft doesn't appear to be. let me check closer and I'll get back shortly. I,ll go bang around on it a bit, its a throw away column.<BR>Coy<P>OK, It is. <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/column.JPG">  <BR>Note in the photo the the tube is telescopic and can move about 5 inches before the lower attachment points hit the larger tube. The shaft is solid from the steering wheel and is fitted with a matching tube. a probe in the tube portion measures about 8 inches.<BR> Is this a kit application? Spyder maybe. <P>[This message has been edited by Wolfhound (edited 05-18-2001).]</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Wolfhound<BR>Yes this is a F355 rebody using the original Ferrari dash which requires the steering to be moved back approx 5".<P>I sure do appreciate any help you can give me.<P>Bruce<BR>88GT<P>||||reg||1
